<title>GERMANY: Daimler says return on capital now 5-6 pct.</title>
<headline>Daimler says return on capital now 5-6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG chief financial officer Manfred Gentz said on Wednesday that the group's return on capital employed now stands at five to six percent.</p>
<p>Gentz told Daimler's annual news conference that the group will have to double its operating profit in order to reach its stated goal of achieving 12 percent return on capital employed.</p>
<p>Earlier, Daimler management board chairman Juergen Schrempp said the group would be able to achieve the 12 percent goal within the next two years.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
